# Security AppSec (Auto — SharePoint ASPX/JS)

Defers to `.cursorrules` Safety; SPFx skill refs win on SPFx/PnPjs details.

- **Secrets**: never hardcode credentials/keys/tokens/connection strings, never commit `.env`/tenant secrets, never log passwords/tokens/session ids
- **Input/Output**: sanitize input, escape output (HTML attr/text/URL contexts) · no `eval`/unchecked `innerHTML` with user data/shell `exec` on user data · prefer textContent/safe DOM APIs
- **AuthZ**: least privilege for admin/script surfaces · prefer host SharePoint auth over invented custom auth
- **Dependencies**: no new packages without need + approval · prefer in-tree JS/host APIs, skill-guided PnPjs defaults
- **PII**: treat names/emails/scores/leaderboard identity as sensitive, never expose in front-end globals or HTML comments
- **Never**: weaken security "to sound less serious" · touch production secrets or expose Local/tenant credentials in replies
